# Copy this to .env and adjust. Docker Compose reads .env automatically.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Compose uses these ONLY to interpolate ${VARIABLES} in the compose files;
# they are not injected into containers automatically. Each service lists the
# variables it actually receives.
#
# Maintenance rule: when you add a variable to .env, add it here in the same
# commit, with a placeholder - never a real value.

# --- Database ---
DATABASE_USER=postgres
# Dev only. Production reads its password from ./secrets/db_password instead
# (see the Production section below), so this stays a dev-only convenience.
DATABASE_PASSWORD=postgres
# Dev defaults to financial_tracking_dev, prod to financial_tracking_prod.
# Override here if you want a specific name.
# DATABASE_NAME=financial_tracking_dev
# Tests use their own database and their own variable (config/test.exs ignores
# DATABASE_NAME on purpose so tests can never touch the dev/prod database).
# TEST_DATABASE_NAME=financial_tracking_test

# Host port for the dev database. Defaults to 15432 because a native
# PostgreSQL install commonly already owns 5432. Inside the compose network
# the app always reaches it as db:5432 regardless of this value.
# DB_HOST_PORT=15432

# --- Livebook (dev) ---
# Shared Erlang cookie used by both the Phoenix node and Livebook so Livebook
# can attach to the running app. Any non-empty string; keep it consistent.
LIVEBOOK_COOKIE=financial_tracking_cookie
# Livebook runs arbitrary Elixir INSIDE the app node, with Repo and every
# context in scope. It is bound to 127.0.0.1, but set a real password anyway
# if you share this machine. Minimum 12 characters.
LIVEBOOK_PASSWORD=financial-tracking-dev-change-me

# --- Production ---
# The host browsers will use to reach the app. REQUIRED - config/runtime.exs
# raises without it, because Phoenix validates LiveView WebSocket origins
# against this value and a stale default silently rejects every socket.
PHX_HOST=localhost

# How the OUTSIDE WORLD reaches the app. The local prod rehearsal serves plain
# HTTP on :4000; behind a real TLS-terminating proxy, delete both of these so
# they fall back to https / 443.
PHX_SCHEME=http
PHX_URL_PORT=4000

# Host interface the prod rehearsal publishes on. Loopback by default so a
# local rehearsal is not reachable from the network. Set to 0.0.0.0 only when
# something in front of it is actually terminating TLS.
# PHX_BIND_IP=127.0.0.1

# Image tag used by compose.prod.yaml. Once images are built in CI, point this
# at the registry reference (preferably pinned by digest) instead.
# IMAGE_TAG=local

# NOTE: SECRET_KEY_BASE and the production DATABASE_PASSWORD are NOT set here.
# They are file-backed secrets, mounted into the containers from ./secrets/
# (gitignored) so their values never appear in `docker inspect`, in a process
# environment, or in `docker compose config` output. Generate them with:
#
#   ./scripts/gen-secrets.sh
#
# Rotating secret_key_base logs out every user.

# --- Optional prod tuning, read by config/runtime.exs ---
# POOL_SIZE=10
# ECTO_IPV6=false
# DNS_CLUSTER_QUERY=
